1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:09,300
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,400
Thanks, Michelle.

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:20,800
I hope you like it.

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,500
Isn't this baby outfit adorable?

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,100
With his name on it--"Max."

6
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:29,300
Thanks so much, Harry and Michelle.

7
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,900
We really appreciate it.

8
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:31,900
I'm glad you like it.

9
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,800
Michelle picked it out.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,400
Yes, I told Daddy to pick blue ones.

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,900
Blue is for boys, and pink is for girls.

12
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,300
And Max is some boy.

13
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,702
He's a real Stewart.

14
00:00:41,702 --> 00:00:43,400
Right.

15
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,000
That was so thoughtful of you, Michelle.

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,900
Especially to pick it out in blue.

17
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,700
Would you like to see baby Max, Michelle?

18
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,100
Could she? Could we?

19
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,711
Could I?

20
00:00:54,711 --> 00:00:56,100
Take them upstairs, Susan.

21
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,866
Harry and Michelle can watch Max sleeping.

22
00:00:57,866 --> 00:01:01,700
Let's go.

23
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,853
Come on, Michelle.

24
00:01:04,853 --> 00:01:06,100
Before Max wakes up.

25
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:07,900
Will you please take this upstairs, Susan?

26
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:08,100
Uh-huh.

27
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:12,900
Thank you.

28
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:17,137
Michelle is very grown up for a ten-year-old, huh?

29
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:20,795
She's smart and sensitive for her age.

30
00:01:20,795 --> 00:01:23,300
Growing up without a mother is difficult.

31
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:26,600
You mature quickly.

32
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:29,900
Susan's like a mother to Michelle.

33
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:33,504
They have a good relationship.

34
00:01:33,504 --> 00:01:39,200
Do you think Susan and Harry will get married?

35
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:42,100
Yeah. You can count on it.

36
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:45,296
I think so. Yes. They get along so well.

37
00:01:45,296 --> 00:01:49,100
I like him. He's good for Susan.

38
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,900
He's a little quiet.

39
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:55,300
It's hard to do anything but listen in this family.

40
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,500
You're right, Ellen.

41
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:02,500
Oh, really?

42
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,056
It's the way it should be.

43
00:02:04,056 --> 00:02:05,464
The Stewarts are the Stewarts!

44
00:02:05,464 --> 00:02:06,700
They always were,

45
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,100
and they always will be.

46
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:08,300
Right!

47
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,600
They've always got an opinion.

48
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,600
Always got something to say.

49
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,700
And now there's Max Stewart.

50
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:18,434
and if he talks as loudly as he cries,

51
00:02:18,434 --> 00:02:20,400
we're all in for trouble.

52
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,200
He's quiet now.

53
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:35,300
Mmm-hmm. That's because he's sleeping.

54
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,900
He's really cute.

55
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,600
It's not necessary to whisper, Harry.

56
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,100
A baby gets used to voices.

57
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,000
I remember now.

58
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,500
We always whispered when Michelle was born.

59
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,300
And I didn't sleep well, Daddy told me.

60
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,100
I never slept.

61
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:48,600
And when I did,

62
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,700
I woke up when I heard someone speak.

63
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:52,460
I bet you were cute.

64
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:53,600
She sure was.

65
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,700
Not as cute as Max.

66
00:02:54,700 --> 00:03:09,500
He's like a little doll.

67
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,600
Oh, good.

68
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,200
Now I can help diaper him.

69
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:18,400
Let's get Marilyn.

70
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,712
What do you do when he cries like that?

71
00:03:19,712 --> 00:03:23,200
You pick him up.

72
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:28,175
He's so little ... so new.

73
00:03:28,175 --> 00:03:31,957
Let's call Marilyn.

74
00:03:31,957 --> 00:04:00,435
Time for a feeding and time for a diapering.

75
00:04:00,435 --> 00:04:03,435
You're a real Stewart.
